

                   ADVENTURER-KINGS:  GAME 3, TURN 2

                                  FOR

                   SHAMAN UGA-BUGA MAKUMBU





              
                              




  Quote of the Week:

  Martin Luther, German theologian and reformer, 1525:
  "In my opinion it is better that all of the peasants should be killed 
rather than that the sovereigns and magistrates should be destroyed, because 
the peasants take up the sword without God's authorization."


ACTION REPORT    

Here's what happened to Your Majesty this turn:


  With the coming of the spring season Uga-Buga Makumb set out to quench his 
thirst for glory.  He left the 108th Skeletal Bowmen, the 109th 
Heavy Cavalry, the 110th Bowmen, the 209th Warg Riders, the 240th Bowmen and 
the 241st Bowmen with Guerin in the Jellyfish Sea.
  Windy spring was followed by early summer.  Uga-Buga Makumb travelled to 
the Virgo Sea.
  In late summer, Melantheus was magically charmed by Uga-Buga Makumb.  
Uga-Buga Makumb bit his fangs into Melantheus and drained all his blood.  
Melantheus changed to Undead alignment!
  With the coming of the fall season Uga-Buga Makumb rode into the Mermaid 
Sea.
  The fall season cooled into early winter.  Uga-Buga Makumb failed in his 
attempt to cast a Charm spell.

  Thus endeth the adventures of Shaman Uga-Buga Makumb Stuffy doll for this 
year.


  Uga-Buga Makumb treated with his ally Lord Babba Sissoko Master orango 
(#0).  Shaman Uga-Buga Makumb Stuffy doll has been informed by Prometeo (#5) 
that his cooperation has become expendable, and thus our formerly friendly 
relations are now severed.
  Shaman Uga-Buga Makumb Stuffy doll has been notified by Giovanna d'Arco 
(#7) that his cooperation has become expendable, and thus our previously 
amicable relations are now broken.

  Your Majesty, I have news to report of wanderers in our kingdom:  
  Raiden (#96) hiked into the Virgo Sea.  He had grown bored with Gafsa and 
was drawn there by rumors of its wonderful wines.
  Odysseus (#97) has arrived in the Mermaid Sea from Tebessa, attracted by 
the great (or terrible?)   reputation of its king.


  Here is the financial report for Uga-Buga Makumb's kingdom: this turn, the 
Kingdom collected 40 gold in revenue.  10 gold was expended to finance our 
leaders.  16 gold was expended to maintain our armies.  Uga-Buga Makumb was 
left with 22 gold in the treasury.


LETTER REPORTS

  O King of Kings, thy heroes have travelled around the globe in
search of adventure and conquest.  I have faithfully kept their
correspondence, and now I present it to thee:


From: Guerin
To: Uga-Buga Makumb

  Honored Sovereign, 

  Winter melted into sweet spring.  I travelled to the Jellyfish Sea.  I saw 
no marauding monsters.
  In early summer, I spoke urgently to Tao-Li and convinced him to pledge 
his allegiance to Uga-Buga Makumb.  After talking to Tao-Li, I judged him (a 
Dwarf well known for Tactics) to have an Evil, Brave character.
  With the advent of the late summer season I marched on Falkenheim (#1106) 
with my command.  Looking to the east, one can see a Forest area, which is 
known as Hollabrand (#1206).  It is populated by Humans and Kokocala rules 
there.  Their Human warriors array themselves as Legion and Chariots.  
Southeast of here is Florence (#1207), a Mountain area owned by 
Lord Babba Sissoko Master orango, where Dwarves dwell.  Their Dwarven 
warriors prefer to array themselves in the style of Axemen and Light Cavalry.

  An army coming from the empire of Shaman Uga-Buga Makumb Stuffy doll 
invaded Falkenheim, hoping to conquer that province ruled by the provincial 
Eagle chieftain and made up of extensive Forests.  I commanded the invading 
armies.  The defending forces were led by the provincial Eagle chieftain.  
The armies were drawn up into lines of battle as shown here:

  ATTACKING ARMY, Battle of Falkenheim (1106):

  110th   
  Bowmen  
