----------
    GC    
 123rd/A  
  Eagles  
          
  DEFENDING ARMY

  The attackers had the 240th Bowmen, the 209th Warg Riders and the 109th 
Heavy Cavalry in reserve.  I led my armies into the fray.  No generals were 
present to lead the forces of the provincial Eagle chieftain.
  The Skeletal Armies led by Uga-Buga Makumb marched into battle with a 
fanatical fervor.  Luckily for me, a force of opportunistic bandits ambushed 
the provincial Eagle chieftain's supply elements, giving me a clear 
advantage.  As the desperate battle developed, the tactical wit of the 
provincial Eagle chieftain and I appeared to be well matched.

  Across the entire front, the Veteran 108th Skeletal Bowmen were arrayed 
against the 123rd Eagles.  The 110th Bowmen and the 240th Bowmen outflanked 
the undermanned enemy and attacked with full strength.  The 123rd Eagles 
swooped down on the 108th Skeletal Bowmen and attacked without mercy.  The 
123rd Eagles were riddled with fire of their feared Bowmen enemy.  The 108th 
Skeletal Bowmen fought with the 123rd Eagles and mowed them down like weeds.
  Guerin's armies vanquished the army opposing them with a final charge.  
The 108th Skeletal Bowmen scattered the 123rd Eagles in all directions.
  Guerin's campaign effected the conquest of Falkenheim.  The battle 
affected the quality of our forces:  the 240th Bowmen proved its mettle 
during the battle and we now rate it a Veteran unit.
  The sultry days of summer surrendered to fall.  I failed in my attempt to 
cast a Bless spell.
  In early winter, I moved into Mare Tarkium (#1107) with my high-spirited 
army.  To the southeast there is a Plain province known as the Maldive Sea 
(#1108), a land of Humans where Lord Babba Sissoko Master orango rules.  
Their Human fighters fight as Legion and Heavy Cavalry.  Viewing the 
southwestern horizon, one can see a Mountain province known as Erg Iguidi 
(#1008).  It is said that Saladin reigns there.  It is known to be occupied 
by Humans.  Their Human warriors traditionally array themselves as Legion 
and Chariots.

  A conquering horde owing their allegiance to 
Shaman Uga-Buga Makumb Stuffy doll invaded the province of Mare Tarkium, a 
Forest area owned by the provincial Dragon chieftain.  I was in command of 
the invading armies.  The defenders were led by the provincial Dragon 
chieftain.  The armies were drawn up into lines of battle as shown here:

  ATTACKING ARMY, Battle of Mare Tarkium (1107):

