  DEFENDING ARMY

  The attackers had the 110th Bowmen, the 209th Warg Riders and the 109th 
Heavy Cavalry in reserve.  I led my armies into the fray.  No generals were 
present to lead the forces of the provincial Dragon chieftain.
  The Skeletal Armies led by Uga-Buga Makumb marched into battle with a 
fanatical fervor.  No luck of any noteworthy significance seemed to 
influence the overall battle before it started.  In this perilous chess 
match, I appeared to gain the tactical edge.

  Across the entire front, the Veteran 108th Skeletal Bowmen faced the 124th 
Dragons.  The 241st Bowmen and the 110th Bowmen flanked the undermanned 
enemy lines and attacked with full force.  The 124th Dragons swooped down on 
the 108th Skeletal Bowmen and attacked them.  The 124th Dragons were 
decimated by the arrows loosed by those dangerous Bowmen.  The 108th 
Skeletal Bowmen battled the 124th Dragons and trampled them down as if they 
were invalids.
  The battle ended in victory for the soldiers of Guerin as they broke 
through at a critical moment.  The 108th Skeletal Bowmen slew the 124th 
Dragons almost to a man.
  Guerin's host concluded the campaign successfully and conquered Mare 
Tarkium.  The battle affected the quality of our forces:  the 240th Bowmen 
was greatly inspired by the victory.  We now designate it a proud Crack 
unit.

  Thy humble servant,   Guerin


From: Teleko
To: Uga-Buga Makumb

  Honored Sovereign, 

  With the advent of the spring season, I prepared to quench my thirst for 
adventure.  My attempted cast of the Oratory spell didn't work.
  Windy spring was followed by early summer.  I travelled to the Mermaid Sea.
Southwest of here lies the province of the Near-Beer Sea (#907), ruled by 
Elmer.  It is known to be a Forest province inhabited by Orcs.  Their Orcish 
fighters prefer to fight as Phalanx and Warg Riders.  To the west lies a 
Forest area named the Buccaneer Sea (#806), populated by Elves.  It is ruled 
by no one.  Their Elven fighters traditionally array themselves in the style 
of Bowmen and Fleet.
  In late summer, I cast a Skeletal Army spell and the 96th Skeletal Bowmen 
arose from the graves of the dead!

  In the Mermaid Sea, Shaman Uga-Buga Makumb Stuffy doll campaigned against 
Lallipugh (#11).  I was in command of the attacking armies.  The defending 
forces were led by Lallipugh.  The armies were drawn up into lines of battle 
as shown here:

  ATTACKING ARMY, Battle of the Mermaid Sea (0906):

 96th/AS  
  Bowmen  
 }}}01}}} 
----------
 |||11||| 
  97th/A  
 Hvy Cav  
          
  DEFENDING ARMY

  Standing tall with my warriors was I.  Lallipugh stood determinedly at the 
head of his thousands.
  The Skeletal Armies led by Uga-Buga Makumb marched into battle with a 
fanatical fervor.  I had used a long flanking march to try to suprise 
Lallipugh.  But the ruse failed, and its only effect was to demoralize 
Teleko's troops.  On the other hand in this slugging match, I seemed to gain 
the tactical edge.

  Across the whole front, the 96th Skeletal Bowmen were arrayed against the 
97th Heavy Cavalry.  In this area, the contest was an uneventful bashing 
match decided by the bravery and ability of the soldiers themselves in 
hand-to-hand combat.  The 96th Skeletal Bowmen battled with the 97th 
Heavy Cavalry and gradually shoved them back.
  The host of Teleko crushed the army of Lallipugh's morale with one last, 
great push.
  Though Teleko's forces were triumphant, Lallipugh rallied his men and 
decided to fight for the Mermaid Sea.  Teleko's efforts improved my prowess 
in Tactics.
  With the coming of the fall season I cast a Skeletal Army spell and no 
skeletons answered the spell's call.

  In the Mermaid Sea, Shaman Uga-Buga Makumb Stuffy doll campaigned against 
Lallipugh.  I was in command of the invading armies.  The defenders were led 
by Lallipugh.  The armies were drawn up into lines of battle as shown here:

  ATTACKING ARMY, Battle of the Mermaid Sea (0906):

 96th/AS  
  Bowmen  
 }}}01}}} 
----------
 |||11||| 
  97th/A  
 Hvy Cav  
          
  DEFENDING ARMY

  I marched with my loyal troops, eyes set in terrible determination.  
Lallipugh led a host of loyal soldiers into the battle.
  The Skeletal Armies led by Uga-Buga Makumb marched into battle with a 
fanatical fervor.  The battle was a fair fight, as no luck of great 
significance appeared to influence the overall result of the battle before 
it commenced.  Teleko's wise tactical maneuvers assured my side an 
undeniable superiority.

  Across the whole front, the 96th Skeletal Bowmen faced the 97th 
Heavy Cavalry.  In this match, the soldiers of the 96th Skeletal Bowmen were 
held up by a muddy field.  Even so, the 96th Skeletal Bowmen fought with the 
97th Heavy Cavalry and determinedly plowed into their opponents.
  Teleko's armies shattered the army opposing them with a final determined 
charge.  The 96th Skeletal Bowmen annihilated the 97th Heavy Cavalry.
  The Mermaid Sea was overrun by the forces of Teleko.
  With the advent of the early winter season I attempted an illegal move.  I 
was ordered to move from the Mermaid Sea to the Icaria Sea, further than my 
army could move.  So, I worked on my Thievery but was frustrated in my 
efforts.

  Thy humble servant,   Teleko


From: Gridley, Squire to Melantheus
To: Uga-Buga Makumb

  Honored Sovereign, 

  The summer surrendered to the fall.  Melantheus tried to improve his 
Sageness, but the task was beyond his ability.  He invented nothing in his 
sagely researches.
  With the coming of the early winter season, Melantheus tried to practice 
his Sageness, but the task seemed beyond his natural aptitude.  He 
discovered nothing in his sagely experiments.

  Thy humble servant,   Gridley, Squire to Melantheus


From: Tao-Li
To: Uga-Buga Makumb

  Honored Sovereign, 

  With the coming of the late summer season I journeyed to the Virgo Sea.  
While adventuring, I saw no wandering monster.
  The summer surrendered to the fall.  I travelled to the Mermaid Sea.  I 
encountered no monster.
  During early winter, I rode into the Icaria Sea.  Looking to the southwest,
one can see a Plain area, which is known as the Shark Sea (#908).  It is 
populated by Orcs and Arnulf rules there.  Their Orcish warriors fight as 
Phalanx and Warg Riders.  During my travels, I was unexpectedly approached 
by a Renegade Archer.  But I hailed the Renegade Archer with friendly words, 
and a fight was averted.


  Thy humble servant,   Tao-Li


